// Regression: poc.downloadProgress((downloaded, total, percent) => {...}) is a
// yaklib call site whose argument count is smaller than the callback's
// parameter list. Resolving the side-effect of the captured `total` looked the
// callback's parameters up in that call's args and aborted the whole compile
// with "parameter index 1 out of bounds for call N (args=1)".
//
// The callback never runs here (registration only), so the assertion checks
// both that the compile succeeds and that registration has no side effect.
total = 0
progress = poc.downloadProgress((downloaded, total, percent) => {
    total = percent
})
assert progress != nil, "downloadProgress must return a usable option"
assert total == 0, "registering a callback must not run it"
